  situationName: The Warning Comes from a Passing Trader
  act: Keep watching the source of the warning from a distance.
  situationDescription: 'The source of the warning eventually crosses an open stretch
    of road: a travelling trader with a loaded pack, moving away from a troubled
    section of the route. They keep glancing back and choose a longer detour. Their
    cargo markings and direction give you a useful clue about conditions affecting
    trade nearby.'
